  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 Ukraine crisis - Winterization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Population Movement and winter shelter</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of the crisis, nearly one third of the total Ukrainians population have been forced from their homes, this marks one of the largest human displacement crises in the world today.
It is estimated that more than 4,1 million people in Ukraine will face extreme winter in 2022-23 and will need external humanitarian assistance</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main winterization activities in with shelter response perspective may include distribution of cash, essential household items and insulation items, support to collective centres accommodating IDPs, support to public services and infrastructure, light and medium repair of houses damaged by the conflict</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine and neigbouring countries</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">more than 4,1 million people in Ukraine (and neighbouring countries)</narrative>
  </description>
